WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.830
- Hi, I'm Toby and welcome
to another exam review video.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.180
So imagine over a million
students applying to take an exam

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.870
for which there are less than 1000 spots

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.960
waiting for them at the end.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.050
This insane competitiveness
is the reality for students

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.930
who are taking India's UPSC exam,

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.480
making it one of the
toughest exams in the world.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.130
So I have some of the UPSC
exam papers here today,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.960
but this isn't even all of it.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.120
It's a huge exam.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.670
It takes up to two years of preparation,

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.810
and when everything's said and done,

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.700
if you make it all the way through,

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.570
you would have sat 32
hours worth of exams.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.430
I've covered some other tough
exams coming out of India

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:51.300
like the JEE advanced
exam for engineering,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.700
or the NEET exam for medical students.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.950
But this UPSC exam is different

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.720
in the fact that you
need to be more on top

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.840
of all your subjects from technology

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.820
to current affairs to philosophy,

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.450
the scope is extremely broad.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.440
UPSC stands for union
Public Service Commission.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.640
And the exam recruits
graduates who have already done

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.760
a university degree who
want to come and work

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.170
for the Indian Civil Services.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.930
So that's basically working
for the Indian government

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.450
in various administrative roles.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.560
It's a highly sought after position,

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.890
and people who do really well on this exam

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.980
are really admired by their fellow peers.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.550
So let's have a look at
the kind of questions

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.980
that would be involved.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.960
The exams held in multiple stages,

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.740
there is the prelims that are two papers,

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.370
general studies and an aptitude test.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:48.820
And if you make it through that,

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.850
it's the main section.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:55.850
Now the mains consists of nine
papers each three hours long,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.760
and this is what they cover.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.180
There are two that are just
qualifying an English exam

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.620
and an exam in an Indian
language of choice.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.620
But then we have an essay
for general studies exams

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.700
and two papers of your choice.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.890
These papers of your choice
are on optional subjects

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.460
which range everything from
physics, maths, philosophy,

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.550
engineering, but also
basically every subject

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.560
you could imagine.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.120
So, let's have a look at
a few of these papers.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.560
So I've got here the first
general studies paper

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.940
this one covers Indian heritage, culture,

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.320
history, geography of the world.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.140
And so everything written
in Hindi and English.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.980
There are 20 questions in this booklet

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.720
and all questions are compulsory

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.873
So let's have a look.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.210
They're not joking that
this is a lot of work.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.730
All of these questions are
little like mini essay questions.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.670
Yeah, like this is kind of Indian history.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.870
Things about an 1857 uprising.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.790
The linkages between The 19th
century Indian Renaissance

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.913
and the emergence of national identity.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.880
So everything from that to
the impact of global warming

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.860
on the coral life system.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.170
What makes Indian society unique

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.360
and sustaining its culture
discuss in 150 words.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.940
So I think, what you really need to do

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.830
to prepare for an exam like this,

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.020
where it's kinda testing
your general knowledge

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:26.990
and I've seen many preparing
students talk about this,

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.270
it's actually reading newspapers.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.900
And reading newspapers
to prepare for an exam

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.700
seems kind of bizarre to me,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.730
but it makes sense.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.960
Newspaper should give
you a pretty good idea

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.060
of what's kind of going
on in the world right?

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.880
So this is another General Studies paper.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.950
Number four, this one should cover ethics,

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.870
integrity and aptitude.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.000
They wanna know what
are the basic principles

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.860
of public life illustrate
any three of these

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.970
with suitable examples?

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:57.550
What do you understand by the
term public servant, right?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:58.740
That's very relevant since

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.570
that's the job you're applying for.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:01.960
But then, we even have some kind

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.360
of philosophical ideas over here.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.520
An unexamined life is not
worth living, socrates

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.360
discuss that in 150 words,

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.420
one from Gandhi, a man is
but a product of his thoughts

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.750
what he thinks he becomes.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:21.060
I'm left feeling that someone
who's prepared for an exam

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.280
like this wouldn't just be
good at sitting this exam

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.290
but they'd be a really knowledgeable

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.130
and smart citizen of the world.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:29.963
You know what I mean?

00:04:29.963 --> 00:04:34.170
Like questions like this on
history, philosophy, geography,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.060
general knowledge are
that they have general

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.050
your tested on them kind
of everyday in your life,

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.150
there are what allows you to contribute

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.480
to interesting discussions with
random people that you meet,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.070
and I don't think this
knowledge would be lost

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.950
when you finish this exam.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:51.220
I think some of these ideas

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.490
just help you understand the world better.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.680
And even if you don't get in,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.380
it's kind of like you
haven't wasted your time.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.730
You spend all this time
becomes knowledgeable

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.080
about your country.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.580
And I don't think that's
something to be upset about.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:10.200
So this is the essay paper of
between 1000 and 1200 words

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.010
on something like wisdom finds truth

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.630
or biased media is a real
threat to Indian democracy,

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.670
or the rise of artificial intelligence.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.710
You see, some of these ideas
are interesting to think about.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.890
Now, that's kind of a look
through the general studies

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.780
and my thoughts on those.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.650
Let's have a look at some
of the optional papers now.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:32.080
So since this is basically
a physics channel,

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.300
I picked a couple of the
optional physics papers.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.360
I've got physics paper
one and physics paper two.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.185
And so let's have a little
bit of a look through these.

00:05:41.185 --> 00:05:43.770
They're starting off not too difficult.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.870
What is the central
force give two examples.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.880
How does Reynolds number help
in the study of fluid motion?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.800
What I noticed straight away is that these

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.690
are not multi choice questions,

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.660
which was the case

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.870
for some of the other
Indian exams I looked at.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.920
This page is pretty interesting Section B.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.690
You answering these physics questions

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.160
in about 150 words each,

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.760
so you have to really be good

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.750
at your communication of scientific ideas.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.900
For example, we're asked
to discuss in brief

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.350
the ultraviolet catastrophe.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.860
How did Planck solve this problem?

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.990
Alright so that's paper one of the six.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.740
Let's have a little look at paper two

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.630
before we make any judgments.

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:25.030
This is starting off with some
quantum mechanics questions.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.100
Again, a lot of explainer type questions.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.210
How do you define density of states?

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:33.870
Define mathematically the Bohr radius.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.140
Calculate the numerical
values for the hydrogen atom.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.030
I should mention that
if you make it through

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.990
all of these papers, you make
it through the main round,

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.350
then there is an interview
and that interview

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.840
would be a bit of a personality test.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.130
So even if you ace all of these,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.720
I guess it's still possible
that you're not quite

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.020
what they were looking for.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:56.040
And that interview is
probably maybe one of the most

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.610
subjective parts of all it's hard

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:01.080
to put a number on someone's personality.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.520
Just like I did in my in my NEET exam

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.630
I'll give this exam, a little rating.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:10.890
So name UPSC the scope.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:15.000
Well, we covered everything
from philosophy to physics.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.160
That's a pretty big scope.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.680
It gets an A and a plus.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.960
Difficulty well, it's a tough exam

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.180
I'll give it an A.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.130
I guess the difficulty will
depend on your strengths

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:30.010
and weaknesses and how
prepared you are feeling

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.720
and how much preparation
you've done for it.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.430
Time pressure, well, it's
kind of a test of stamina,

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.170
this is such a long process.

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:43.320
Like I said, you would have
done 32 hours of examinations.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.180
If you've done all of these papers,

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:50.180
the interview, the mains,
that prelims, that's intense.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.440
In terms of actual time pressure yet,

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.270
you have three hours to
answer heaps of questions

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.070
I'll give it an A as well.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.660
Now the big one competitiveness.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.970
This is the most competitive exam

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.910
I've ever covered on the channel.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.020
I thought NEET was competitive,

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.970
but students here are competing
for only hundreds of spots.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.770
So this is going to be A
never before seen rating

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:17.070
of A plus plus, plus plus.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.550
And that's what makes this one
of the most difficult exams.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.570
If you want me to compare it overall

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:24.750
to the JEE advanced exam,

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:29.700
I would say that UPSC is tougher
on the basis of selection,

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.550
but JEE advanced was probably tougher

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.150
on the basis of the questions,

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.020
but they are two totally different exams,

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.760
testing different things
for different people

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.640
who want different jobs.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.850
I wanted to finish this
video with a little story.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:50.850
So I printed out these UPSC
exam papers at the library.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.040
And while I was doing so,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.650
there was some of the pages
got caught in the printer

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:56.920
and there was a little printer jam

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:58.640
you might be able to see this page here

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.010
is a bit crinkled.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:03.090
Anyway, one of the staff
members at the library

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.150
came over to help.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.710
And as he was fishing these pages out

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.190
from inside the printer,

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.217
he recognized the exam and he asked me,

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:13.860
"are you preparing for UPSC?"

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.180
You see, he said he was from India

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.400
and he himself had prepared for the UPSC.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.050
I told him that "no I
wasn't preparing for it."

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.300
And it was a little bit hard to explain

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.960
what I was doing printing it out

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.670
if I had no interest in sitting it myself.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.420
But he ended up telling me his story

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.450
about how he'd done a lot
of preparation himself

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.950
when he used to live in India,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.620
and he'd gotten quite
far through the exam.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.130
He's done quite well,
but he didn't make it

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:41.370
all the way to the end.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.220
So he'd faced the disappointment

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.880
of not getting through the UPSC.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.690
But life had taken him
on a different journey.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.220
He'd gone to university in
India and studied languages

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.200
and even done a PhD.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:58.790
I guess that PhD had allowed
him to apply for a job

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.900
in Australia at the
library and he was living

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.820
a happy life here.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.500
So it was kind of a
coincidence for me to bump

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.440
into a UPSC alumni here in Australia.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.720
But there were two things I
kind of took away from it.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:18.690
One was that UPSC is so
widely known in India

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.420
and so many people apply for it

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:23.780
that you might bump into
people who have done it

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.450
anywhere around the world,

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.700
but also that UPSC and passing it

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.240
is not everything and that

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.820
there are multiple paths to happiness.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.230
Even if you try really
hard to pass an exam

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.210
and you think you want to take your life

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:39.740
in a certain direction.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.420
There are other directions that life

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:44.360
could take you even if you
don't get what you want.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.170
Sometimes not getting what you want

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.810
can even be a wonderful stroke of luck.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.140
So keep that in mind.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:51.640
And thank you for watching.

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:54.223
(gentle music)

